<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gretl-functions>
<gretl-function-package name="EViewsCompat" minver="2026a">
<author>EViewsCompat contributors</author>
<version>0.3</version>
<date>2026-11-15</date>
<description>EViews-style LS, NLS, ARMA, systems, VAR/VEC, forecasts, Wald, diagnostics and at-functions</description>
<tags>C10 C20 C51</tags>
<label>EViews-style equation (LS)</label>
<menu-attachment>MAINWIN/Model/LinearModels</menu-attachment>
<help>
EViewsCompat: EViews-style estimation and functions for gretl

GUI: Model &gt; Linear models &gt; EViews-style equation (LS)
  Type the equation exactly as in EViews' &quot;Equation Estimation&quot; box, e.g.
      dlog(lrm) c dlog(lry) lrm(-1) ibo ide
  and select (at least) the series the equation uses. The result window
  shows the EViews-style table; its graph button draws Actual/Fitted/Residual.
  Save the result as an icon to keep it in the session (like an EViews
  workfile object).

Note: hansl names are case-sensitive, so type series names as they appear
in gretl. EViews keywords (c, log, d, dlog, the @-functions) are not.

Functions (CLI / console). &quot;dataset&quot; means: all series in the dataset.

  ev_ls(spec, dataset [, cov] [, quiet])  -&gt; bundle
      Least squares. spec in EViews syntax. cov: &quot;ordinary&quot; (default),
      &quot;white&quot; or &quot;hac&quot;. Prints the EViews-style table unless quiet = 1.
      Supported terms: c, x, x(-k), log(x), d(x), dlog(x), exp(), abs(),
      sqr(), any gretl expression, @trend, @seas(k), @pch, @pc,
      @pchy, @pcy, @movav(x,n), @movsum(x,n), @cumsum,
      @mean, @stdev.
      Bundle members: coeff, stderr, tstat, pval, vcv, rsq, adjrsq, sigma,
      ssr, lnl, dw, aic, sc, hq, F, Fp, T, k, uhat, yhat, y, X, sample.
      aic/sc/hq use EViews' per-observation scaling (gretl value / T).

  ev_wald(eq, &quot;c(2)=0, c(3)=c(4)&quot;)      -&gt; bundle (F, Fp, chi2, chi2p)
      Linear coefficient restrictions in EViews c(i) notation.

  ev_diag(eq [, lags])                  -&gt; bundle
      Jarque-Bera, Breusch-Godfrey LM (default 2 lags), White test with
      cross terms; F and Obs*R-squared versions as in EViews.

  ev_freeze(eq, &quot;file.csv&quot;)             save table (.txt .csv .tex .html)
      Relative names are written in the gretl working directory.

  ev_print(&amp;eq), ev_plot(&amp;eq)           print table / Actual-Fitted-Residual

  ev_gen(&quot;expr&quot;, dataset)               EViews expression -&gt; series
  ev_trend(), ev_seas(k), ev_pch(x), ev_pc(x), ev_pchy(x), ev_pcy(x),
  ev_movav(x,n), ev_movsum(x,n), ev_mean(x), ev_stdev(x) (n-1),
  ev_var(x) (population, n), ev_obs(x), ev_elem(x, &quot;1990:1&quot;)

Forecasts (eq.forecast). The forecast sample is the current sample.

  ev_forecast(eq, dataset [, dynamic=1] [, quiet])   -&gt; bundle
      Static (0) or dynamic (1). Dynamic forecasts replace lags of a plain
      dependent variable, y(-k), by earlier forecasts. Bundle: yf, se,
      actual, rmse, mae, mape, theil, bias_prop, var_prop, cov_prop.
  series f = ev_fcast_series(fc)     series s = ev_fcast_se(fc)
  ev_fplot(&amp;fc [, &quot;file.png&quot;])       forecast with +/- 2 S.E. and actual

VAR objects (var v.ls 1 2 y1 y2 @ c x)

  ev_varest(&quot;1 2 y1 y2 @ c x&quot;, dataset [, quiet] [, &quot;names&quot;])  -&gt; bundle
      Lag pairs (1 2 = lags 1 to 2), endogenous variables, then exogenous
      after the at-sign; c = constant (included by default when there is no
      exogenous part). Use series names so lags can use pre-sample data;
      &quot;names&quot; gives display names, e.g. &quot;dlog(cons) dlog(gdp)&quot;.
  ev_varprint(&amp;v)               EViews-style estimates: coef, (s.e.), [t]
  ev_vargranger(v)              Granger causality / block exogeneity Wald
  ev_varirf(v, 10)              impulse responses (Cholesky)
  ev_varirfplot(v, 10 [, &quot;file.png&quot;])   grid of response graphs
  ev_vardecomp(v, 10)           variance decomposition (percent)
  ev_varlaglen(v, dataset, 8)   lag length criteria
  series r = ev_varresid(v, 1)  residuals of equation 1

Explicit equations, ARMA terms (ev_ls dispatches automatically)

  ev_ls(&quot;y = c(1) + c(2)*x^c(3)&quot;, dataset)    nonlinear least squares
  ev_ls(&quot;y c x ar(1) ar(4) ma(1)&quot;, dataset)    regression with ARMA errors (ML)
      ARMA output shows SIGMASQ and the inverted AR/MA roots. Forecasts of
      either kind use the same ev_forecast call.

Forecasts of transformed dependents

  ev_forecast(eq, dataset, 1, 0, 1)   dynamic forecast reported in levels:
      for log(Y), d(Y), dlog(Y) the forecast of Y is built step by step and
      every regressor that uses Y is recomputed. ev_fcast_series(fc, 1) and
      ev_fcast_se(fc, 1) give the level forecast and its S.E. Dynamic S.E.
      follow the lags of the dependent variable (innovation uncertainty).

Systems (system sys1 / sys1.sur)

  ev_system(deps, xspecs, cnums, dataset, &quot;sur&quot; [, &quot;z1 z2&quot;])
      deps: array of dependent variables; xspecs: regressors per equation
      (&quot;c x1 x2&quot;); cnums: coefficient numbers per equation (&quot;1 2 3&quot;); the same
      number in two equations shares the coefficient. Methods ls, sur, tsls,
      3sls; instruments get a constant added. ev_wald works with c(i).

VEC models (var v.ec(c, 1) 1 2 y1 y2)

  ev_vecm(&quot;1 2 y1 y2 [@ x]&quot;, dataset, &quot;c&quot;, 1)   trend case a-e, rank
  ev_coint(&quot;y1 y2&quot;, dataset, &quot;c&quot;, 4)            Johansen test
      The VAR views (ev_varirf, ev_varirfplot, ev_vardecomp) work on VEC results.
</help>
<gretl-function name="ev_gen" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="expr" type="string">
<description>EViews expression, e.g. dlog(y)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series referenced in the expression</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># Evaluate an EViews-syntax expression and return the series.
string evx_e = ev__prep(expr, vars)
if instring(evx_e, &quot;ev_&quot;)
  # expression calls package functions: catch is not allowed here
  series evx_out = @evx_e
else
  catch series evx_out = @evx_e
endif
errorif($error, sprintf(&quot;Cannot evaluate '%s' (hansl: %s). Check the series names and that they are in the list you passed.&quot;, expr, evx_e))
return evx_out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ls" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation, e.g. y c x x(-1)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list" optional="true">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ordinary, white or hac</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Suppress printed output</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!exists(vars), &quot;Pass the series to use as second argument, e.g. ev_ls(\&quot;y c x\&quot;, dataset)&quot;)
string evx_cov = exists(cov) ? tolower(cov) : &quot;ordinary&quot;
# explicit form y = c(1) + c(2)*x  -&gt; nonlinear least squares
if instring(spec, &quot;=&quot;)
  return ev_nls(spec, vars, evx_cov, quiet)
endif
# ARMA error terms ar(k) / ma(k) -&gt; regression with ARMA errors (exact ML)
if regsub(tolower(&quot; &quot; ~ spec ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;.*\s(ar|ma)\([0-9]+\)\s.*&quot;, &quot;ARMA&quot;) == &quot;ARMA&quot;
  return ev_arma(spec, vars, quiet)
endif
errorif(!instring(&quot; ordinary white hac &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ evx_cov ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;cov must be ordinary, white or hac&quot;)
strings evx_tok = strsplit(spec)
errorif(nelem(evx_tok) &lt; 2, &quot;The specification needs a dependent variable and at least one regressor&quot;)

series evx_y = ev_gen(evx_tok[1], vars)
list evx_X = null
strings evx_lab = array(0)
scalar evx_hascon = 0
loop evx_i = 2..nelem(evx_tok)
  string evx_t = evx_tok[evx_i]
  if tolower(evx_t) == &quot;c&quot;
    list evx_X += const
    evx_lab += &quot;C&quot;
    evx_hascon = 1
  else
    string evx_v = sprintf(&quot;evx_r%d&quot;, evx_i)
    series @evx_v = ev_gen(evx_t, vars)
    list evx_X += @evx_v
    evx_lab += toupper(evx_t)
  endif
endloop

scalar evx_n0 = $nobs
if evx_cov == &quot;white&quot;
  set force_hc on
  ols evx_y evx_X --robust --quiet
elif evx_cov == &quot;hac&quot;
  errorif($datatype != 2, &quot;HAC covariance needs time-series data&quot;)
  ols evx_y evx_X --robust --quiet
else
  ols evx_y evx_X --quiet
endif

bundle b
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(evx_tok[1])
b.labels = evx_lab
b.covtype = evx_cov
b.coeff = $coeff
b.stderr = $stderr
b.vcv = $vcv
b.T = $T
b.k = $ncoeff
b.rsq = $rsq
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - $rsq) * ($T - 1) / ($T - $ncoeff)
b.sigma = $sigma
b.ssr = $ess
b.lnl = $lnl
b.dw = $dw
b.hascon = evx_hascon
b.adjusted = $T &lt; evx_n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)

series evx_u = $uhat
series evx_f = $yhat
smpl ok(evx_u) --restrict
b.y = {evx_y}
b.X = {evx_X}
b.uhat = {evx_u}
b.yhat = {evx_f}
series evx_o = obs
b.tobs = {evx_o}
b.sample =sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))

scalar n = b.T
scalar k = b.k
matrix d = b.y - meanc(b.y)
b.meany = meanc(b.y)
b.sdy = sqrt(d'd / (n - 1))
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + k * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k * log(log(n)) / n
if evx_hascon &amp;&amp; k &gt; 1
  b.F = (b.rsq / (k - 1)) / ((1 - b.rsq) / (n - k))
  b.Fp = pvalue(F, k - 1, n - k, b.F)
else
  b.F = NA
  b.Fp = NA
endif
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix p = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  p[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, n - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = p

if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_print" type="void" pkg-role="bundle-print">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result&quot;)
printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar
printf &quot;Method: %s\n&quot;, inbundle(b, &quot;method&quot;) ? b.method : &quot;Least Squares&quot;
printf &quot;Date: %s\n&quot;, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample
printf &quot;Included observations: %d%s\n&quot;, b.T, b.adjusted ? &quot; after adjustments&quot; : &quot;&quot;
if b.covtype == &quot;white&quot;
  printf &quot;White heteroskedasticity-consistent standard errors &amp; covariance\n&quot;
elif b.covtype == &quot;hac&quot;
  printf &quot;HAC standard errors &amp; covariance (Bartlett kernel, Newey-West)\n&quot;
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;eqline&quot;)
  printf &quot;%s\n&quot;, b.eqline
endif
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
matrix ord = inbundle(b, &quot;order&quot;) ? b.order : seq(1, b.k)
loop r = 1..cols(ord)
  scalar i = ord[r]
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
endloop
if inbundle(b, &quot;sigmasq&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, &quot;SIGMASQ&quot;, b.sigmasq, b.sigmasq_se, b.sigmasq / b.sigmasq_se, 2 * pvalue(t, b.T - b.k, abs(b.sigmasq / b.sigmasq_se))
endif
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;R-squared&quot;, b.rsq, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.meany
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Adjusted R-squared&quot;, b.adjrsq, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.sdy
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;S.E. of regression&quot;, b.sigma, &quot;Akaike info criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, b.ssr, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl, &quot;Hannan-Quinn criter.&quot;, b.hq
if ok(b.F)
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, b.F, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, b.dw
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Prob(F-statistic)&quot;, b.Fp
else
  printf &quot;%-22s%14s    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, b.dw
endif
ev__line(78)
if inbundle(b, &quot;ar_roots&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-22s%s\n&quot;, &quot;Inverted AR Roots&quot;, b.ar_roots
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;ma_roots&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-22s%s\n&quot;, &quot;Inverted MA Roots&quot;, b.ma_roots
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;ar_roots&quot;) || inbundle(b, &quot;ma_roots&quot;)
  ev__line(78)
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_plot" type="void" pkg-role="bundle-plot">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code># EViews View &gt; Actual, Fitted, Residual
errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;uhat&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result&quot;)
matrix M = b.y ~ b.yhat ~ b.uhat
cnameset(M, defarray(&quot;Actual&quot;, &quot;Fitted&quot;, &quot;Residual&quot;))
gnuplot 1 2 3 --matrix=M --time-series --with-lines --y2axis=3 --output=display {set title &quot;Actual, Fitted, Residual&quot;; set ylabel &quot;Actual / Fitted&quot;; set y2label &quot;Residual&quot;;}
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wald" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="restr" type="string">
<description>Restrictions, e.g. c(2)=0, c(3)=0</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an ev_ls result&quot;)
strings R = strsplit(restr, &quot;,&quot;)
scalar J = nelem(R)
scalar k = b.k
scalar n = b.T
matrix Rm = zeros(J, k)
matrix q = zeros(J, 1)
# coefficient numbers: c(i) is the i-th coefficient, except in systems
# where the numbers used may have gaps
matrix cpos = inbundle(b, &quot;cnums&quot;) ? b.cnums : seq(1, k)
scalar K = maxr(cpos)
matrix evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
loop j = 1..J
  strings sides = strsplit(R[j], &quot;=&quot;)
  errorif(nelem(sides) != 2, sprintf(&quot;Restriction '%s' must contain exactly one '='&quot;, R[j]))
  string ex = sprintf(&quot;(%s)-(%s)&quot;, sides[1], sides[2])
  ex = regsub(ex, &quot;(?i)\bc\(([0-9]+)\)&quot;, &quot;evw_c[\1]&quot;)
  matrix idx = {}
  evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
  catch scalar f0 = @ex
  errorif($error, sprintf(&quot;Cannot parse restriction '%s' (coefficients are c(1)..c(%d))&quot;, R[j], k))
  loop i = 1..k
    evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
    evw_c[cpos[i]] = 1
    Rm[j, i] = (@ex) - f0
  endloop
  # linearity check at a random point
  matrix rc = mnormal(k, 1)
  evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
  evw_c[cpos] = rc
  errorif(abs((@ex) - (Rm[j,] * rc + f0)) &gt; 1e-8 * (1 + abs(f0)), sprintf(&quot;Restriction '%s' is not linear&quot;, R[j]))
  q[j] = -f0
endloop
matrix dev = Rm * b.coeff - q
scalar W = qform(dev', inv(qform(Rm, b.vcv)))
bundle w
w.restr = restr
w.chi2 = W
w.chi2p = pvalue(X, J, W)
w.F = W / J
w.Fp = pvalue(F, J, n - k, w.F)
w.df1 = J
w.df2 = n - k
w.R = Rm
w.q = q
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nWald Test:\nEquation: %s\n\n&quot;, b.spec
  printf &quot;%-20s%14s%14s%14s\n&quot;, &quot;Test Statistic&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Probability&quot;
  printf &quot;%-20s%14.6f%14s%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, w.F, sprintf(&quot;(%d, %d)&quot;, J, n - k), w.Fp
  printf &quot;%-20s%14.6f%14d%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Chi-square&quot;, w.chi2, J, w.chi2p
  printf &quot;\nNull Hypothesis: %s\n\n&quot;, toupper(restr)
endif
return w
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_diag" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nlags" type="int" min="1" default="2">
<description>Serial correlation LM nlags</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;uhat&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an ev_ls result&quot;)
matrix u = b.uhat
matrix Xm = b.X
scalar n = rows(u)
scalar k = cols(Xm)
bundle r

# Jarque-Bera
matrix uc = u - meanc(u)
scalar m2 = meanc(uc.^2)
r.skew = meanc(uc.^3) / m2^1.5
r.kurt = meanc(uc.^4) / m2^2
r.jb = n / 6 * (r.skew^2 + (r.kurt - 3)^2 / 4)
r.jbp = pvalue(X, 2, r.jb)

# Breusch-Godfrey (presample residuals set to zero, as EViews)
matrix UL = zeros(n, nlags)
loop j = 1..nlags
  UL[j+1:n, j] = u[1:n-j]
endloop
scalar ssr0 = 0
scalar df0 = 0
scalar ssr1 = 0
scalar df1 = 0
scalar r2 = ev__fit(u, Xm ~ UL, &amp;ssr1, &amp;df1)
ev__fit(u, Xm, &amp;ssr0, &amp;df0)
r.bg_lags = nlags
r.bg_obsr2 = n * r2
r.bg_chi2p = pvalue(X, nlags, r.bg_obsr2)
r.bg_F = ((ssr0 - ssr1) / nlags) / (ssr1 / (n - df1))
r.bg_Fp = pvalue(F, nlags, n - df1, r.bg_F)

# White test with cross terms
matrix nc = selifc(Xm, sdc(Xm) .&gt; 1e-12)
matrix Z = ones(n, 1) ~ nc
loop i = 1..cols(nc)
  loop j = i..cols(nc)
    Z ~= nc[,i] .* nc[,j]
  endloop
endloop
scalar ssrw = 0
scalar dfw = 0
scalar r2w = ev__fit(u.^2, Z, &amp;ssrw, &amp;dfw)
scalar m = dfw - 1
r.white_obsr2 = n * r2w
r.white_df = m
r.white_chi2p = pvalue(X, m, r.white_obsr2)
r.white_F = (r2w / m) / ((1 - r2w) / (n - dfw))
r.white_Fp = pvalue(F, m, n - dfw, r.white_F)

if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nResidual Diagnostics\nEquation: %s\n&quot;, b.spec
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;Normality: Jarque-Bera\n&quot;
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    Prob.%21.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Jarque-Bera&quot;, r.jb, r.jbp
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-14s%12.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Skewness&quot;, r.skew, &quot;Kurtosis&quot;, r.kurt
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;Breusch-Godfrey Serial Correlation LM Test (%d lags)\n&quot;, nlags
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.bg_F, sprintf(&quot;Prob. F(%d,%d)&quot;, nlags, n - df1), r.bg_Fp
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Obs*R-squared&quot;, r.bg_obsr2, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, nlags), r.bg_chi2p
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;Heteroskedasticity Test: White (with cross terms)\n&quot;
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.white_F, sprintf(&quot;Prob. F(%d,%d)&quot;, m, n - dfw), r.white_Fp
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Obs*R-squared&quot;, r.white_obsr2, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, m), r.white_chi2p
  ev__line(70)
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_freeze" type="void">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="fname" type="string">
<description>Output file: .txt, .csv, .tex or .html</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an ev_ls result&quot;)
string ext = tolower(regsub(fname, &quot;.*\.&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
if ext == &quot;txt&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    ev_print(&amp;b)
  end outfile
elif ext == &quot;csv&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    printf &quot;Variable,Coefficient,Std. Error,t-Statistic,Prob.\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..b.k
      printf &quot;\&quot;%s\&quot;,%.10g,%.10g,%.10g,%.10g\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\nR-squared,%.10g\nAdjusted R-squared,%.10g\nS.E. of regression,%.10g\n&quot;, b.rsq, b.adjrsq, b.sigma
    printf &quot;Sum squared resid,%.10g\nLog likelihood,%.10g\nDurbin-Watson stat,%.10g\n&quot;, b.ssr, b.lnl, b.dw
    printf &quot;Akaike info criterion,%.10g\nSchwarz criterion,%.10g\nIncluded observations,%d\n&quot;, b.aic, b.sc, b.T
  end outfile
elif ext == &quot;tex&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    printf &quot;\\begin{tabular}{lrrrr}\n\\hline\n&quot;
    printf &quot;Variable &amp; Coefficient &amp; Std. Error &amp; t-Statistic &amp; Prob. \\\\\n\\hline\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..b.k
      printf &quot;%s &amp; %.6f &amp; %.6f &amp; %.4f &amp; %.4f \\\\\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\\hline\nR-squared &amp; %.6f &amp; &amp; Durbin-Watson &amp; %.4f \\\\\n&quot;, b.rsq, b.dw
    printf &quot;Observations &amp; %d &amp; &amp; S.E. of regression &amp; %.6f \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{tabular}\n&quot;, b.T, b.sigma
  end outfile
elif ext == &quot;html&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    printf &quot;&lt;table border=\&quot;1\&quot; cellpadding=\&quot;4\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;caption&gt;Dependent Variable: %s (%s)&lt;/caption&gt;\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.sample
    printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Variable&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Coefficient&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Std. Error&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;t-Statistic&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Prob.&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..b.k
      printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;%s&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.4f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.4f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
    endloop
    printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;R-squared&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan=\&quot;2\&quot;&gt;Durbin-Watson stat&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.4f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&quot;, b.rsq, b.dw
    printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Observations&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%d&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan=\&quot;2\&quot;&gt;S.E. of regression&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;\n&quot;, b.T, b.sigma
  end outfile
else
  funcerr &quot;Unsupported extension: use .txt, .csv, .tex or .html&quot;
endif
printf &quot;Frozen table written to %s\n&quot;, fname
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_trend" type="series">
<code>series t = obs - 1
return t
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_seas" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="k" type="int" min="1"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(k &gt; $pd, sprintf(&quot;Season %d exceeds data frequency %d&quot;, k, $pd))
series s = $obsminor == k
return s
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pch" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return x / x(-1) - 1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pc" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return 100 * (x / x(-1) - 1)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pchy" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return x / x(-$pd) - 1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pcy" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return 100 * (x / x(-$pd) - 1)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_movav" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="n" type="int" min="1"/>
 </params>
<code>if n == 1
  return x
endif
return movavg(x, n)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_movsum" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="n" type="int" min="1"/>
 </params>
<code>if n == 1
  return x
endif
return n * movavg(x, n)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_mean" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return mean(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_stdev" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># sample standard deviation (n-1), as EViews
return sd(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_var" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># population variance (divisor n), as EViews
return sd(x)^2 * (nobs(x) - 1) / nobs(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_obs" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return nobs(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_elem" type="scalar">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="ob" type="string">
<description>Observation, e.g. 1990:1</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return x[obsnum(ob)]
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fit" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;tobs&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result (or estimated with an older EViewsCompat)&quot;)
return ev__toseries(b.yhat, b.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_resid" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;tobs&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result (or estimated with an older EViewsCompat)&quot;)
return ev__toseries(b.uhat, b.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_forecast" type="bundle">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool" default="1">
<description>Dynamic (1) or static (0)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="level" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Report the level of the dependent variable, e.g. Y for dlog(Y)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an equation (ev_ls result)&quot;)
string kind = inbundle(b, &quot;kind&quot;) ? b.kind : &quot;ls&quot;
string dep = kind == &quot;nls&quot; ? b.lhs : strsplit(b.spec)[1]
string base = &quot;&quot;
scalar form = ev__depform(dep, &amp;base, vars)
series evf_y = ev_gen(dep, vars)
matrix y = {evf_y}
series evf_o = obs
matrix tobs = {evf_o}
scalar T = rows(y)
scalar k = b.k
matrix beta = b.coeff
scalar s2 = b.sigma^2

# actual level and its previous value (pre-sample visible through the lag)
matrix Ylev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix Yprev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
if form &gt;= 0
  string e1 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base
  string e2 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(-1)&quot;
  series evf_L = @e1
  series evf_Lp = @e2
  Ylev = {evf_L}
  Yprev = {evf_Lp}
endif

# how the right-hand side is evaluated
strings tok = array(0)
matrix X = {}
matrix usesY = {}
if kind == &quot;arma&quot;
  return ev__fc_arma(b, vars, dynamic, quiet, level, form, base)
elif kind == &quot;nls&quot;
  loop j = 1..k
    string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, b.cidx[j])
    scalar @pn = beta[j]
  endloop
  string rhx = ev__prep(b.rhs, vars)
  series evf_r0 = @rhx
  matrix r0 = {evf_r0}
  # gradient for the coefficient part of the S.E.
  matrix J = {}
  loop j = 1..k
    string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, b.cidx[j])
    scalar h = 1e-6 * (1 + abs(beta[j]))
    scalar @pn = beta[j] + h
    series evf_rp = @rhx
    scalar @pn = beta[j]
    J ~= ({evf_rp} - r0) / h
  endloop
else
  tok = strsplit(b.spec)
  loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
    if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
      series evf_r = 1
    else
      series evf_r = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    endif
    X ~= {evf_r}
    scalar u_ = form &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; regsub(tok[i], &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;#&quot;) != tok[i]
    usesY ~= u_
  endloop
  errorif(cols(X) != k, &quot;Could not rebuild the regressors of the equation&quot;)
endif

# AR terms in the dependent variable -&gt; psi weights for multi-step S.E.
matrix phi = zeros(1, 24)
scalar dyn_ok = dynamic &amp;&amp; form &gt;= 0
if kind == &quot;ls&quot; &amp;&amp; form &gt;= 0
  string dl = tolower(regsub(dep, &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
  loop L = 1..24
    string cand = regsub(dl, &quot;(?&lt;![a-z0-9_])&quot; ~ tolower(base) ~ &quot;(?![a-z0-9_])&quot;, tolower(base) ~ sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, L))
    if form == 0
      cand = tolower(base) ~ sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, L)
    endif
    loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
      if tolower(regsub(tok[i], &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;)) == cand
        phi[L] = beta[i-1]
      endif
    endloop
  endloop
endif
matrix psi = zeros(T, 1)
psi[1] = 1
loop j = 2..T
  loop L = 1..min(24, j - 1)
    psi[j] += phi[L] * psi[j - L]
  endloop
endloop
matrix psiC = cum(psi)

# step through the forecast sample
matrix yf = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix se = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix yfl = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix sel = mshape(NA, T, 1)
series evf_dlt = 0          # forecast minus actual level (dynamic forecasts)
loop t = 1..T
  scalar v = NA
  scalar st = tobs[t]
  matrix g = {}
  if kind == &quot;nls&quot;
    v = r0[t]
    if dyn_ok &amp;&amp; t &gt; 1
      series evf_rr = ev__gen2(b.rhs, vars, base, evf_dlt)
      v = evf_rr[st]
    endif
    g = J[t,]
  else
    matrix x = X[t,]
    if dyn_ok &amp;&amp; t &gt; 1
      loop i = 1..cols(x)
        if usesY[i]
          series evf_rc = ev__gen2(tok[i+1], vars, base, evf_dlt)
          if ok(evf_rc[st])
            x[i] = evf_rc[st]
          endif
        endif
      endloop
    endif
    if sum(!ok(x)) == 0
      v = x * beta
    endif
    g = x
  endif
  if !ok(v)
    continue
  endif
  yf[t] = v
  scalar h = dynamic ? t : 1
  # static: innovation and coefficient uncertainty; dynamic: innovation
  # uncertainty propagated through the lags of the dependent variable (as gretl)
  scalar cvar = (!dynamic &amp;&amp; sum(!ok(g)) == 0) ? qform(g, b.vcv) : 0
  se[t] = sqrt(s2 * sumc(psi[1:h].^2) + cvar)
  if form &gt;= 0
    scalar prev = (t &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; dynamic &amp;&amp; ok(yfl[t-1])) ? yfl[t-1] : Yprev[t]
    if form == 0
      yfl[t] = v
      sel[t] = se[t]
    elif form == 1
      yfl[t] = exp(v)
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * se[t]
    elif form == 2
      yfl[t] = prev + v
      sel[t] = dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t]
    else
      yfl[t] = prev * exp(v)
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * (dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t])
    endif
    if dyn_ok
      evf_dlt[st] = yfl[t] - Ylev[t]
    endif
  endif
endloop
return ev__fc_finish(b, dep, base, form, dynamic, level, y, yf, se, Ylev, yfl, sel, tobs, quiet, kind == &quot;nls&quot; &amp;&amp; dynamic)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="f" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>string nm = f.level ? f.base : f.depvar
printf &quot;\nForecast: %sF\nActual: %s\n&quot;, f.level ? f.base : f.depvar, nm
printf &quot;Forecast sample: %s\n&quot;, f.sample
printf &quot;Method: %s\n&quot;, f.dynamic ? &quot;Dynamic forecast&quot; : &quot;Static forecast&quot;
printf &quot;Included observations: %d\n&quot;, f.nobs
if f.nobs &gt; 0
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Root Mean Squared Error&quot;, f.rmse
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Mean Absolute Error&quot;, f.mae
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Mean Abs. Percent Error&quot;, f.mape
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Theil Inequality Coef.&quot;, f.theil
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;     Bias Proportion&quot;, f.bias_prop
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;     Variance Proportion&quot;, f.var_prop
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;     Covariance Proportion&quot;, f.cov_prop
endif
if f.se_note != &quot;&quot;
  printf &quot;Note: %s\n&quot;, f.se_note
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fcast_series" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="f" type="bundle">
<description>ev_forecast result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="level" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Level of the dependent variable</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(level ? f.yfl : f.yf, f.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fcast_se" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="f" type="bundle">
<description>ev_forecast result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="level" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Level of the dependent variable</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(level ? f.sel : f.se, f.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fplot" type="void">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="f" type="bundleref"/>
  <param name="fname" type="string" optional="true"/>
 </params>
<code># forecast with +/- 2 S.E. bands, and the actual series
matrix p = f.level ? f.yfl : f.yf
matrix s = f.level ? f.sel : f.se
matrix a = f.level ? f.actual_level : f.actual
matrix M = p ~ (p + 2 * s) ~ (p - 2 * s) ~ a
cnameset(M, defarray(&quot;Forecast&quot;, &quot;+2 S.E.&quot;, &quot;-2 S.E.&quot;, &quot;Actual&quot;))
string out = exists(fname) ? fname : &quot;display&quot;
gnuplot 1 2 3 4 --matrix=M --time-series --with-lines --single-yaxis --output=&quot;@out&quot; {set title &quot;Forecast with +/- 2 S.E.&quot;;}
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_depbase" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>Equation (ev_ls result)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># the series Y when the dependent variable is log(Y), d(Y) or dlog(Y); &quot;&quot; otherwise
string dep = inbundle(b, &quot;lhs&quot;) ? b.lhs : strsplit(b.spec)[1]
string base = &quot;&quot;
scalar f = ev__depform(dep, &amp;base, vars)
return f &gt; 0 ? base : &quot;&quot;
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varest" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Lag pairs, endogenous, then exogenous after the at-sign</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="names" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Display names for the variables, space separated</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># Plain series names are used directly, so lags reach before the sample start
# as in gretl's var. Expressions are evaluated inside this function, where
# pre-sample values are not available: create them as series first if that matters.
string AT = &quot;@&quot;
strings LB = exists(names) ? strsplit(names) : array(0)
scalar nexpr = 0
strings parts = strsplit(spec, AT)
errorif(nelem(parts) &gt; 2, &quot;Use the at-sign once, before the exogenous variables&quot;)
strings L = strsplit(parts[1])
# leading integers are lag pairs
matrix lagv = {}
scalar i0 = 1
loop while i0 + 1 &lt;= nelem(L) &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0+1], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
  scalar a = atof(L[i0])
  scalar z = atof(L[i0+1])
  errorif(a &lt; 1 || z &lt; a, &quot;Lag pairs must be like 1 2 (from 1 to 2)&quot;)
  lagv ~= seq(a, z)
  i0 += 2
endloop
errorif(cols(lagv) == 0, &quot;Start the specification with lag pairs, e.g. 1 2&quot;)
lagv = values(lagv')'
errorif(nelem(L) - i0 + 1 &lt; 1, &quot;No endogenous variables&quot;)
list Y = null
strings ylab = array(0)
strings ytok = array(0)
strings xtok = array(0)
loop i = i0..nelem(L)
  matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), L[i])
  if rows(pp) &gt; 0
    list Y += vars[pp[1]]
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evv_y%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(L[i], vars)
    list Y += @v
    nexpr++
  endif
  scalar li = nelem(ytok) + 1
  ylab += nelem(LB) &gt;= li ? toupper(LB[li]) : toupper(L[i])
  ytok += L[i]
endloop
list X = null
strings xlab = array(0)
scalar hasc = nelem(parts) == 1   # no exogenous part: constant by default
if nelem(parts) == 2
  strings R = strsplit(parts[2])
  loop i = 1..nelem(R)
    if tolower(R[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
      hasc = 1
    else
      matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), R[i])
      if rows(pp) &gt; 0
        list X += vars[pp[1]]
      else
        string v = sprintf(&quot;evv_x%d&quot;, i)
        series @v = ev_gen(R[i], vars)
        list X += @v
        nexpr++
      endif
      scalar li = nelem(ytok) + nelem(xtok) + 1
      xlab += nelem(LB) &gt;= li ? toupper(LB[li]) : toupper(R[i])
      xtok += R[i]
    endif
  endloop
endif
scalar n0 = $nobs
if nelem(X) &gt; 0
  if hasc
    var lagv Y ; X --silent
  else
    var lagv Y ; X --silent --nc
  endif
else
  if hasc
    var lagv Y --silent
  else
    var lagv Y --silent --nc
  endif
endif
bundle sys = $system
if nexpr &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; !quiet
  printf &quot;Note: %d variable(s) given as expressions lose their pre-sample lags;\n&quot;, nexpr
  printf &quot;      create them as series first to use the full sample.\n&quot;
endif

bundle b
b.spec = spec
b.sys = sys
b.ylab = ylab
b.xlab = xlab
b.ytok = ytok
b.xtok = xtok
b.lags = lagv
b.hasc = hasc
b.n = nelem(Y)
b.T = sys.T
b.k = sys.ncoeff
b.coeff = sys.coeff
b.adjusted = sys.T &lt; n0
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(sys.t1), obslabel(sys.t2))
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
# coefficient labels in gretl's order: const, lagv of each endogenous, exogenous
strings clab = array(0)
if hasc
  clab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
loop j = 1..b.n
  loop l = 1..cols(lagv)
    clab += sprintf(&quot;%s(-%d)&quot;, ylab[j], lagv[l])
  endloop
endloop
loop j = 1..nelem(xlab)
  clab += xlab[j]
endloop
errorif(nelem(clab) != b.k, &quot;Internal error: coefficient labels do not match&quot;)
b.clab = clab

# per-equation statistics
scalar T = b.T
scalar k = b.k
matrix E = sys.uhat
matrix Ym = sys.Y
matrix ssr = sumc(E.^2)
matrix dev = Ym .- meanc(Ym)
matrix sst = sumc(dev.^2)
b.ssr = ssr
b.rsq = 1 - ssr ./ sst
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - b.rsq) * (T - 1) / (T - k)
b.seeq = sqrt(ssr / (T - k))
b.se = sqrt(diag(sys.xtxinv)) * b.seeq       # k x n
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.se
b.Fstat = hasc ? (b.rsq / (k - 1)) ./ ((1 - b.rsq) / (T - k)) : mshape(NA, 1, b.n)
b.lnl_eq = -T / 2 * (1 + log(2 * $pi) + log(ssr / T))
b.aic_eq = -2 * b.lnl_eq / T + 2 * k / T
b.sc_eq = -2 * b.lnl_eq / T + k * log(T) / T
b.meany = meanc(Ym)
b.sdy = sqrt(sst / (T - 1))
matrix S = E'E / T
b.det_adj = det(E'E / (T - k))
b.det = det(S)
b.lnl = sys.lnl
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / T + 2 * b.n * k / T
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / T + b.n * k * log(T) / T
if !quiet
  ev_varprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;sys&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_varest result&quot;)
scalar n = b.n
printf &quot;\nVector Autoregression Estimates\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample
printf &quot;Included observations: %d%s\n&quot;, b.T, b.adjusted ? &quot; after adjustments&quot; : &quot;&quot;
printf &quot;Standard errors in ( ) &amp; t-statistics in [ ]\n\n&quot;
scalar w = 22 + 16 * n
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
loop j = 1..n
  printf &quot;%16s&quot;, b.ylab[j]
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
# EViews order: lags first, then C, then exogenous
matrix ord = {}
scalar c0 = b.hasc ? 2 : 1
scalar nl = b.n * cols(b.lags)
ord ~= seq(c0, c0 + nl - 1)
if b.hasc
  ord ~= 1
endif
if b.k &gt; nl + b.hasc
  ord ~= seq(c0 + nl, b.k)
endif
loop r = 1..cols(ord)
  scalar i = ord[r]
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, b.clab[i]
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, b.coeff[i,j]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;(%.5f)&quot;, b.se[i,j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;[%.5f]&quot;, b.tstat[i,j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n\n&quot;
endloop
ev__line(w)
strings nm = defarray(&quot;R-squared&quot;, &quot;Adj. R-squared&quot;, &quot;Sum sq. resids&quot;, &quot;S.E. equation&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, &quot;Akaike AIC&quot;, &quot;Schwarz SC&quot;, &quot;Mean dependent&quot;, &quot;S.D. dependent&quot;)
matrices st = defarray(b.rsq, b.adjrsq, b.ssr, b.seeq, b.Fstat, b.lnl_eq, b.aic_eq, b.sc_eq, b.meany, b.sdy)
loop r = 1..nelem(nm)
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, nm[r]
  matrix v = st[r]
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, v[j]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
endloop
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant resid covariance (dof adj.)&quot;, b.det_adj
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant resid covariance&quot;, b.det
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Akaike information criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
ev__line(w)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vargranger" type="matrix">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># VAR Granger causality / block exogeneity Wald tests (chi-square), EViews style.
# Returns rows: dependent j, excluded i (0 = all), chi2, df, p
scalar n = b.n
scalar p = cols(b.lags)
scalar c0 = b.hasc ? 2 : 1
matrix V0 = b.sys.xtxinv
matrix out = {}
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nVAR Granger Causality/Block Exogeneity Wald Tests\nSample: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, b.sample, b.T
endif
loop j = 1..n
  if !quiet
    printf &quot;\nDependent variable: %s\n\n%-22s%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, b.ylab[j], &quot;Excluded&quot;, &quot;Chi-sq&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  endif
  scalar s2 = b.seeq[j]^2
  matrix allidx = {}
  loop i = 1..n
    if i != j
      matrix idx = seq(c0 + (i - 1) * p, c0 + i * p - 1)
      allidx ~= idx
      matrix bb = b.coeff[idx, j]
      scalar W = qform(bb', inv(s2 * V0[idx, idx]))
      out |= {j, i, W, p, pvalue(X, p, W)}
      if !quiet
        printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, b.ylab[i], W, p, pvalue(X, p, W)
      endif
    endif
  endloop
  if n &gt; 1
    matrix bb = b.coeff[allidx, j]
    scalar W = qform(bb', inv(s2 * V0[allidx, allidx]))
    out |= {j, 0, W, cols(allidx), pvalue(X, cols(allidx), W)}
    if !quiet
      printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;All&quot;, W, cols(allidx), pvalue(X, cols(allidx), W)
    endif
  endif
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varirf" type="matrix">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="10">
<description>Horizon</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Impulse responses (Cholesky, one S.D. innovations). Column (s-1)*n+t holds
# the response of variable t to a shock in variable s.
scalar n = b.n
set horizon h
matrix R = {}
loop s = 1..n
  loop t = 1..n
    matrix r = irf(t, s, 0, b.sys)
    R ~= r[1:h, 1]
  endloop
endloop
if !quiet
  loop t = 1..n
    printf &quot;\nResponse of %s:\n%-8s&quot;, b.ylab[t], &quot;Period&quot;
    loop s = 1..n
      printf &quot;%16s&quot;, b.ylab[s]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..h
      printf &quot;%-8d&quot;, i
      loop s = 1..n
        printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, R[i, (s - 1) * n + t]
      endloop
      printf &quot;\n&quot;
    endloop
  endloop
  printf &quot;\nCholesky ordering: &quot;
  loop s = 1..n
    printf &quot;%s &quot;, b.ylab[s]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
endif
return R
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varirfplot" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="10"/>
  <param name="fname" type="string" optional="true"/>
 </params>
<code># grid of impulse-response graphs: row = responding variable, column = shock
matrix R = ev_varirf(b, h, 1)
scalar n = b.n
strings plots = array(0)
loop t = 1..n
  loop s = 1..n
    matrix M = R[, (s - 1) * n + t]
    string ttl = sprintf(&quot;Response of %s to %s&quot;, b.ylab[t], b.ylab[s])
    string buf = &quot;&quot;
    gnuplot 1 --matrix=M --time-series --with-lines --outbuf=buf {set title &quot;@ttl&quot; font &quot;,9&quot;; unset key; set xlabel &quot;&quot;; set ylabel &quot;&quot;; set xzeroaxis lt 1 lc rgb &quot;#c0392b&quot;;}
    plots += buf
  endloop
endloop
string out = exists(fname) ? fname : &quot;display&quot;
gridplot plots --rows=n --width=900 --height=700 --fontsize=9 --output=&quot;@out&quot;
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vardecomp" type="matrix">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="10"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Variance decomposition in percent; block t holds rows 1..h for variable t
scalar n = b.n
set horizon h
matrix D = {}
loop t = 1..n
  matrix d = fevd(t, 0, b.sys)
  D |= 100 * d[1:h, 1:n]
endloop
if !quiet
  matrix R = ev_varirf(b, h, 1)
  loop t = 1..n
    printf &quot;\nVariance Decomposition of %s:\n%-8s%14s&quot;, b.ylab[t], &quot;Period&quot;, &quot;S.E.&quot;
    loop s = 1..n
      printf &quot;%14s&quot;, b.ylab[s]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..h
      scalar v = 0
      loop s = 1..n
        v += sumc(R[1:i, (s - 1) * n + t].^2)
      endloop
      printf &quot;%-8d%14.6f&quot;, i, sqrt(v)
      loop s = 1..n
        printf &quot;%14.4f&quot;, D[(t - 1) * h + i, s]
      endloop
      printf &quot;\n&quot;
    endloop
  endloop
  printf &quot;\nCholesky ordering: &quot;
  loop s = 1..n
    printf &quot;%s &quot;, b.ylab[s]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
endif
return D
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varlaglen" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="maxlag" type="int" min="1" default="8"/>
 </params>
<code># lag length criteria (gretl's var --lagselect)
list Y = null
loop i = 1..b.n
  string v = sprintf(&quot;evl_y%d&quot;, i)
  series @v = ev_gen(b.ytok[i], vars)
  list Y += @v
endloop
list X = null
loop i = 1..nelem(b.xtok)
  string v = sprintf(&quot;evl_x%d&quot;, i)
  series @v = ev_gen(b.xtok[i], vars)
  list X += @v
endloop
printf &quot;\nVAR Lag Order Selection Criteria\nEndogenous variables: &quot;
loop i = 1..b.n
  printf &quot;%s &quot;, b.ylab[i]
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
if nelem(X) &gt; 0
  if b.hasc
    var maxlag Y ; X --lagselect
  else
    var maxlag Y ; X --lagselect --nc
  endif
elif b.hasc
  var maxlag Y --lagselect
else
  var maxlag Y --lagselect --nc
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varresid" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="i" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Equation number</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>matrix t = seq(b.sys.t1, b.sys.t2)'
return ev__toseries(b.sys.uhat[, i], t)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_nls" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Explicit equation, e.g. y = c(1) + c(2)*x^c(3)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ordinary, white or hac</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string covt = exists(cov) ? tolower(cov) : &quot;ordinary&quot;
strings sides = strsplit(spec, &quot;=&quot;)
errorif(nelem(sides) != 2, &quot;Use exactly one '=' in an explicit equation&quot;)
string lhs = strstrip(sides[1])
string rhs0 = strstrip(sides[2])
string low = tolower(rhs0)
matrix cidx = {}
loop i = 1..99
  if instring(low, sprintf(&quot;c(%d)&quot;, i))
    cidx ~= i
  endif
endloop
errorif(cols(cidx) == 0, &quot;No coefficients c(1), c(2), ... in the equation&quot;)
string rhs = regsub(rhs0, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_])c\(([0-9]+)\)&quot;, &quot;evn_c\1&quot;)
string rhx = ev__prep(rhs, vars)
series evn_y = ev_gen(lhs, vars)
string plist = &quot;&quot;
loop j = 1..cols(cidx)
  string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, cidx[j])
  scalar @pn = 0
  plist ~= &quot; &quot; ~ pn
endloop
scalar n0 = $nobs
if covt == &quot;ordinary&quot;
  nls evn_y = @rhx
    params @plist
  end nls --quiet
else
  nls evn_y = @rhx
    params @plist
  end nls --quiet --robust
endif
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;nls&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.lhs = lhs
b.rhs = rhs
b.cidx = cidx
b.depvar = toupper(lhs)
b.method = &quot;Least Squares (Gauss-Newton / Marquardt steps)&quot;
b.eqline = regsub(toupper(lhs ~ &quot;=&quot; ~ rhs0), &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;)
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..cols(cidx)
  lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, cidx[j])
endloop
b.labels = lab
b.covtype = covt
b.coeff = $coeff
b.stderr = $stderr
b.vcv = $vcv
b.k = $ncoeff
b.lnl = $lnl
b.sigma = $sigma
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
series evn_u = $uhat
series evn_f = $yhat
smpl ok(evn_u) --restrict
b.y = {evn_y}
b.uhat = {evn_u}
b.yhat = {evn_f}
series evn_o = obs
b.tobs = {evn_o}
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
# numerical gradient: used as regressors by the residual diagnostics
matrix J = {}
loop j = 1..b.k
  string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, cidx[j])
  scalar h = 1e-6 * (1 + abs(b.coeff[j]))
  scalar @pn = b.coeff[j] + h
  series evn_fp = @rhx
  scalar @pn = b.coeff[j]
  J ~= ({evn_fp} - b.yhat) / h
endloop
b.X = J
ev__stats(&amp;b)
if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_arma" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation with ar(k) / ma(k) terms, e.g. y c x ar(1) ma(1)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>strings tok = strsplit(spec)
series eva_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
list evaX = null
strings xlab = array(0)
strings xtok = array(0)
scalar hasc = 0
matrix pl = {}
matrix ql = {}
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  string t = tolower(tok[i])
  if t == &quot;c&quot;
    hasc = 1
  elif regsub(t, &quot;^ar\([0-9]+\)$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
    pl ~= atof(regsub(t, &quot;[^0-9]&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
  elif regsub(t, &quot;^ma\([0-9]+\)$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
    ql ~= atof(regsub(t, &quot;[^0-9]&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;eva_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list evaX += @v
    xlab += toupper(tok[i])
    xtok += tok[i]
  endif
endloop
if cols(pl)
  pl = values(pl')'
endif
if cols(ql)
  ql = values(ql')'
endif
matrix eva_pl = pl
matrix eva_ql = ql
string pa = cols(pl) ? &quot;eva_pl&quot; : &quot;0&quot;
string qa = cols(ql) ? &quot;eva_ql&quot; : &quot;0&quot;
scalar n0 = $nobs
# with regressors gretl needs the constant listed explicitly
if hasc &amp;&amp; nelem(evaX) &gt; 0
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y const evaX --quiet
elif hasc
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y --quiet
elif nelem(evaX) &gt; 0
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y evaX --quiet --nc
else
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y --quiet --nc
endif
matrix cf = $coeff
matrix sd = $stderr
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;arma&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.method = &quot;ARMA Maximum Likelihood (BFGS)&quot;
b.covtype = &quot;ordinary&quot;
b.hasc = hasc
b.pl = pl
b.ql = ql
b.xtok = xtok
# gretl order: const, AR, MA, regressors;  EViews order: C, regressors, AR, MA
scalar np = cols(pl)
scalar nq = cols(ql)
scalar nx = nelem(xtok)
strings lab = array(0)
if hasc
  lab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
loop i = 1..np
  lab += sprintf(&quot;AR(%d)&quot;, pl[i])
endloop
loop i = 1..nq
  lab += sprintf(&quot;MA(%d)&quot;, ql[i])
endloop
loop i = 1..nx
  lab += xlab[i]
endloop
b.labels = lab
matrix ord = {}
if hasc
  ord ~= 1
endif
scalar o1 = hasc + np + nq + 1
scalar o2 = hasc + np + nq + nx
scalar o3 = hasc + 1
scalar o4 = hasc + np + nq
if nx
  ord ~= seq(o1, o2)
endif
if np + nq
  ord ~= seq(o3, o4)
endif
b.order = ord
b.coeff = cf
b.stderr = sd
b.vcv = $vcv
b.k = rows(cf)
b.lnl = $lnl
scalar i1 = hasc + 1
scalar i2 = hasc + np
scalar i3 = hasc + np + 1
scalar i4 = hasc + np + nq
scalar i5 = hasc + np + nq + 1
scalar i6 = hasc + np + nq + nx
b.phi = np ? cf[i1:i2]' : {}
b.theta = nq ? cf[i3:i4]' : {}
matrix bb = {}
if hasc
  bb |= cf[1]
endif
if nx
  bb |= cf[i5:i6]
endif
b.beta = bb
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
series eva_u = $uhat
series eva_f = $yhat
smpl ok(eva_u) --restrict
b.y = {eva_y}
b.uhat = {eva_u}
b.yhat = {eva_f}
series eva_o = obs
b.tobs = {eva_o}
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
matrix Xm = hasc ? ones(rows(b.y), 1) : {}
if nx
  Xm ~= {evaX}
endif
b.X = cols(Xm) ? Xm : ones(rows(b.y), 1)
b.ureg = cols(Xm) ? b.y - Xm * bb : b.y
scalar T = rows(b.y)
b.sigmasq = (b.uhat'b.uhat) / T
b.sigmasq_se = b.sigmasq * sqrt(2 / T)
b.sigma = sqrt((b.uhat'b.uhat) / (T - b.k))
if np
  b.ar_roots = ev__roots(b.phi, pl, 1)
endif
if nq
  b.ma_roots = ev__roots(b.theta, ql, -1)
endif
ev__stats(&amp;b)
if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_system" type="bundle">
 <params count="8">
  <param name="deps" type="strings">
<description>Dependent variable of each equation</description>
  </param>
  <param name="xspecs" type="strings">
<description>Regressors of each equation, e.g. c x1 x2</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cnums" type="strings">
<description>Coefficient numbers of each equation, e.g. 1 2 3</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ls, sur, tsls or 3sls</description>
  </param>
  <param name="inst" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Instruments (a constant is added)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="eqtext" type="strings" optional="true">
<description>Equations as written, for the output</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string meth = exists(method) ? tolower(method) : &quot;ls&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; ls ols sur tsls 2sls 3sls &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ meth ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;method must be ls, sur, tsls or 3sls&quot;)
meth = meth == &quot;ols&quot; ? &quot;ls&quot; : (meth == &quot;2sls&quot; ? &quot;tsls&quot; : meth)
scalar n = nelem(deps)
errorif(nelem(xspecs) != n || nelem(cnums) != n, &quot;deps, xspecs and cnums must have one entry per equation&quot;)
# series of every equation, over the current sample
matrix Yall = {}
matrices XX = array(n)
matrices CC = array(n)
loop i = 1..n
  series evs_y = ev_gen(deps[i], vars)
  Yall ~= {evs_y}
  strings tk = strsplit(xspecs[i])
  strings cn = strsplit(cnums[i])
  errorif(nelem(tk) != nelem(cn), sprintf(&quot;equation %d: regressors and coefficient numbers differ&quot;, i))
  matrix Xi = {}
  matrix ci = {}
  loop j = 1..nelem(tk)
    if tolower(tk[j]) == &quot;c&quot;
      series evs_x = 1
    else
      series evs_x = ev_gen(tk[j], vars)
    endif
    Xi ~= {evs_x}
    ci ~= atof(cn[j])
  endloop
  XX[i] = Xi
  CC[i] = ci
endloop
matrix Z = {}
if exists(inst) &amp;&amp; strstrip(inst) != &quot;&quot;
  series evs_one = 1
  Z = {evs_one}
  strings zt = strsplit(inst)
  loop j = 1..nelem(zt)
    if tolower(zt[j]) != &quot;c&quot;
      series evs_z = ev_gen(zt[j], vars)
      Z ~= {evs_z}
    endif
  endloop
endif
errorif((meth == &quot;tsls&quot; || meth == &quot;3sls&quot;) &amp;&amp; cols(Z) == 0, &quot;tsls and 3sls need instruments&quot;)
# balanced sample: rows complete in every equation
matrix okr = sumr(!ok(Yall)) .= 0
loop i = 1..n
  okr = okr .* (sumr(!ok(XX[i])) .= 0)
endloop
if cols(Z)
  okr = okr .* (sumr(!ok(Z)) .= 0)
  Z = selifr(Z, okr)
endif
series evs_o = obs
matrix tobs = selifr({evs_o}, okr)
Yall = selifr(Yall, okr)
scalar T = rows(Yall)
# unique coefficient numbers -&gt; columns of the stacked design
matrix allc = {}
loop i = 1..n
  XX[i] = selifr(XX[i], okr)
  allc ~= CC[i]
endloop
matrix cu = values(allc')'
scalar p = cols(cu)
matrix Xs = zeros(n * T, p)
matrix kk = zeros(1, n)
loop i = 1..n
  matrix ci = CC[i]
  kk[i] = cols(ci)
  loop j = 1..cols(ci)
    scalar col = imaxr(cu .= ci[j])
    scalar r1 = (i - 1) * T + 1
    scalar r2 = i * T
    matrix xij = XX[i]
    Xs[r1:r2, col] += xij[, j]
  endloop
endloop
matrix ys = vec(Yall)
# instruments: project each equation's block
matrix Xh = Xs
if meth == &quot;tsls&quot; || meth == &quot;3sls&quot;
  matrix P = Z * inv(Z'Z) * Z'
  loop i = 1..n
    scalar r1 = (i - 1) * T + 1
    scalar r2 = i * T
    Xh[r1:r2, ] = P * Xs[r1:r2, ]
  endloop
endif
# first stage: equation by equation (OLS or 2SLS), with sandwich covariance
matrix A = inv(Xh'Xs)
matrix b = A * (Xh'ys)
matrix E = mshape(ys - Xs * b, T, n)
matrix S = E'E / T
matrix V = {}
if meth == &quot;ls&quot; || meth == &quot;tsls&quot;
  matrix dfa = sqrt((T - kk)' * (T - kk))
  matrix Sd = (E'E) ./ dfa
  V = A * Xh' * (Sd ** I(T)) * Xh * A'
else
  # SUR / 3SLS: feasible GLS with Sigma from the first stage
  matrix Wi = inv(S) ** I(T)
  V = inv(Xh' * Wi * Xh)
  b = V * (Xh' * Wi * ys)
  E = mshape(ys - Xs * b, T, n)
endif
bundle bs
bs.kind = &quot;system&quot;
bs.method = meth
bs.spec = &quot;system&quot;
bs.coeff = b
bs.vcv = V
bs.stderr = sqrt(diag(V))
bs.cnums = cu
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..p
  lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, cu[j])
endloop
bs.labels = lab
bs.k = p
bs.n = n
bs.Tobs = T
bs.T = n * T                 # total system observations (for Wald F df)
bs.uhat = E
bs.sigma_mat = E'E / T
bs.detS = det(E'E / T)
bs.tobs = tobs
bs.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(tobs)), obslabel(maxc(tobs)))
bs.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
bs.tstat = b ./ bs.stderr
matrix pv = zeros(p, 1)
loop j = 1..p
  pv[j] = 2 * pvalue(t, n * T - p, abs(bs.tstat[j]))
endloop
bs.pval = pv
strings dl = array(0)
loop i = 1..n
  dl += toupper(deps[i])
endloop
bs.deps = dl
if exists(eqtext)
  bs.eqtext = eqtext
else
  bs.eqtext = dl
endif
# per-equation statistics
matrix st = {}
loop i = 1..n
  matrix u = E[, i]
  matrix y = Yall[, i]
  matrix d = y - meanc(y)
  scalar ssr = u'u
  scalar r2 = 1 - ssr / (d'd)
  matrix du = u[2:T] - u[1:T-1]
  st |= {r2, 1 - (1 - r2) * (T - 1) / (T - kk[i]), sqrt(ssr / (T - kk[i])), (du'du) / ssr, meanc(y), sqrt(d'd / (T - 1)), ssr}
endloop
bs.eqstats = st
if !quiet
  ev_sysprint(&amp;bs)
endif
return bs
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_sysprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>strings mname = defarray(&quot;Least Squares&quot;, &quot;Seemingly Unrelated Regression&quot;, &quot;Two-Stage Least Squares&quot;, &quot;Three-Stage Least Squares&quot;)
scalar mi = b.method == &quot;ls&quot; ? 1 : (b.method == &quot;sur&quot; ? 2 : (b.method == &quot;tsls&quot; ? 3 : 4))
printf &quot;\nSystem: %s\nEstimation Method: %s\nDate: %s\n&quot;, inbundle(b, &quot;name&quot;) ? b.name : &quot;UNTITLED&quot;, mname[mi], b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, b.sample, b.Tobs
printf &quot;Total system (balanced) observations %d\n\n&quot;, b.T
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop j = 1..b.k
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[j], b.coeff[j], b.stderr[j], b.tstat[j], b.pval[j]
endloop
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-40s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant residual covariance&quot;, b.detS
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..b.n
  printf &quot;\nEquation: %s\nObservations: %d\n&quot;, b.eqtext[i], b.Tobs
  matrix s = b.eqstats[i,]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;R-squared&quot;, s[1], &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, s[5]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Adjusted R-squared&quot;, s[2], &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, s[6]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;S.E. of regression&quot;, s[3], &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, s[7]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, s[4]
  ev__line(78)
endloop
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_sysresid" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_system result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="i" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Equation number</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(b.uhat[, i], b.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vecm" type="bundle">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Lag pairs of the differences, endogenous, then exogenous after the at-sign</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="tcase" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Trend case a, b, c (default), d or e</description>
  </param>
  <param name="crank" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Number of cointegrating equations</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="names" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Display names, space separated</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string AT = &quot;@&quot;
string cs = exists(tcase) ? tolower(tcase) : &quot;c&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; a b c d e &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ cs ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;trend case must be a, b, c, d or e&quot;)
strings LB = exists(names) ? strsplit(names) : array(0)
strings parts = strsplit(spec, AT)
strings L = strsplit(parts[1])
matrix lagv = {}
scalar i0 = 1
loop while i0 + 1 &lt;= nelem(L) &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0+1], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
  lagv ~= seq(atof(L[i0]), atof(L[i0+1]))
  i0 += 2
endloop
errorif(cols(lagv) == 0, &quot;Start with lag pairs for the differences, e.g. 1 2&quot;)
lagv = values(lagv')'
errorif(lagv[1] != 1 || maxr(lagv) != cols(lagv), &quot;VEC lags must run from 1 without gaps, e.g. 1 2&quot;)
scalar order = maxr(lagv) + 1          # gretl's order counts lags in levels
list Y = null
strings ylab = array(0)
strings ytok = array(0)
loop i = i0..nelem(L)
  matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), L[i])
  if rows(pp) &gt; 0
    list Y += vars[pp[1]]
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evc_y%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(L[i], vars)
    list Y += @v
  endif
  scalar li = nelem(ytok) + 1
  ylab += nelem(LB) &gt;= li ? toupper(LB[li]) : toupper(L[i])
  ytok += L[i]
endloop
errorif(crank &lt; 1 || crank &gt;= nelem(Y), &quot;rank must be between 1 and the number of variables minus 1&quot;)
list X = null
strings xlab = array(0)
if nelem(parts) == 2
  strings R = strsplit(parts[2])
  loop i = 1..nelem(R)
    if tolower(R[i]) != &quot;c&quot;
      matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), R[i])
      if rows(pp) &gt; 0
        list X += vars[pp[1]]
      else
        string v = sprintf(&quot;evc_x%d&quot;, i)
        series @v = ev_gen(R[i], vars)
        list X += @v
      endif
      xlab += toupper(R[i])
    endif
  endloop
endif
string opt = cs == &quot;a&quot; ? &quot;--nc&quot; : (cs == &quot;b&quot; ? &quot;--rc&quot; : (cs == &quot;c&quot; ? &quot;--uc&quot; : (cs == &quot;d&quot; ? &quot;--crt&quot; : &quot;--ct&quot;)))
scalar n0 = $nobs
if nelem(X) &gt; 0
  vecm order crank Y ; X --silent @opt
else
  vecm order crank Y --silent @opt
endif
bundle sys = $system
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;vecm&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.case = cs
b.rank = crank
b.sys = sys
b.ylab = ylab
b.xlab = xlab
b.ytok = ytok
strings noxt = array(0)
b.xtok = noxt
b.lags = lagv
b.hasc = cs == &quot;c&quot; || cs == &quot;d&quot; || cs == &quot;e&quot;
b.n = nelem(Y)
b.T = sys.T
b.coeff = $coeff
b.se = $stderr
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.se
b.beta = $jbeta
b.alpha = $jalpha
b.beta_se = sqrt(abs(diag($jvbeta)))
b.k = rows(b.coeff)
b.adjusted = sys.T &lt; n0
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(sys.t1), obslabel(sys.t2))
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
b.lnl = $lnl
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / b.T + 2 * (b.n * b.k) / b.T
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / b.T + (b.n * b.k) * log(b.T) / b.T
matrix E = sys.uhat
b.det = det(E'E / b.T)
# gretl order: const, lagged differences, exogenous, trend, EC terms
strings clab = array(0)
if b.hasc
  clab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
loop j = 1..b.n
  loop l = 1..cols(lagv)
    clab += sprintf(&quot;D(%s(-%d))&quot;, ylab[j], lagv[l])
  endloop
endloop
loop j = 1..nelem(xlab)
  clab += xlab[j]
endloop
if cs == &quot;e&quot;
  clab += &quot;@TREND&quot;
endif
loop r = 1..crank
  clab += sprintf(&quot;CointEq%d&quot;, r)
endloop
errorif(nelem(clab) != b.k, sprintf(&quot;Internal error: %d labels for %d coefficients&quot;, nelem(clab), b.k))
b.clab = clab
if !quiet
  ev_vecprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vecprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>scalar n = b.n
printf &quot;\nVector Error Correction Estimates\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample
printf &quot;Included observations: %d%s\n&quot;, b.T, b.adjusted ? &quot; after adjustments&quot; : &quot;&quot;
printf &quot;Standard errors in ( ) &amp; t-statistics in [ ]\n\n&quot;
scalar w = 22 + 16 * max(n, b.rank)
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;Cointegrating Eq:&quot;
loop r = 1..b.rank
  printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;CointEq%d&quot;, r)
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
scalar nb = rows(b.beta)
loop i = 1..nb
  string nm = i &lt;= n ? sprintf(&quot;%s(-1)&quot;, b.ylab[i]) : (b.case == &quot;b&quot; ? &quot;C&quot; : &quot;@TREND(-1)&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, nm
  loop r = 1..b.rank
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, b.beta[i, r]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
  # gretl gives the variance of the freely estimated elements only
  scalar fi = (i - b.rank - 1) * b.rank + 1
  if i &gt; b.rank &amp;&amp; rows(b.beta_se) &gt;= fi + b.rank - 1
    printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
    loop r = 1..b.rank
      printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;(%.5f)&quot;, b.beta_se[fi + r - 1])
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
    loop r = 1..b.rank
      printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;[%.5f]&quot;, b.beta[i, r] / b.beta_se[fi + r - 1])
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
  endif
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;Error Correction:&quot;
loop j = 1..n
  printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;D(%s)&quot;, b.ylab[j])
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
# EViews order: CointEq, lagged differences, C, exogenous
scalar k = b.k
matrix ord = seq(k - b.rank + 1, k)
scalar c0 = b.hasc ? 2 : 1
scalar nl = n * cols(b.lags)
ord ~= seq(c0, c0 + nl - 1)
if b.hasc
  ord ~= 1
endif
if k - b.rank &gt;= c0 + nl
  ord ~= seq(c0 + nl, k - b.rank)
endif
loop r = 1..cols(ord)
  scalar i = ord[r]
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, b.clab[i]
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, b.coeff[i, j]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;(%.5f)&quot;, b.se[i, j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;[%.5f]&quot;, b.tstat[i, j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n\n&quot;
endloop
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant resid covariance&quot;, b.det
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Akaike information criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
ev__line(w)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_coint" type="void">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="names" type="string">
<description>Endogenous series, e.g. y1 y2</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="tcase" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Trend case a, b, c (default), d or e</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nlag" type="int" min="1" default="4">
<description>Lags of the differences</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># Johansen cointegration test (gretl's coint2)
string cs = exists(tcase) ? tolower(tcase) : &quot;c&quot;
string opt = cs == &quot;a&quot; ? &quot;--nc&quot; : (cs == &quot;b&quot; ? &quot;--rc&quot; : (cs == &quot;c&quot; ? &quot;&quot; : (cs == &quot;d&quot; ? &quot;--crt&quot; : &quot;--ct&quot;)))
list Y = null
strings L = strsplit(names)
loop i = 1..nelem(L)
  matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), L[i])
  errorif(rows(pp) == 0, sprintf(&quot;%s: use series names for the Johansen test&quot;, L[i]))
  list Y += vars[pp[1]]
endloop
scalar order = nlag + 1
printf &quot;\nJohansen Cointegration Test\nSeries: %s\nLags interval (in first differences): 1 to %d\n&quot;, toupper(names), nlag
coint2 order Y @opt
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ls_gui" type="bundle" pkg-role="gui-main">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation (EViews syntax)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="spec2" type="string" optional="true">
<description>  ...continued (optional)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="spec3" type="string" optional="true">
<description>  ...continued (optional)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used in the equation</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="int" min="1" max="3" default="1">
<description>Coefficient covariance</description>
<labels count="3">
"Ordinary" "White" "HAC (Newey-West)" </labels>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># optional parts may arrive empty or as the literal text &quot;null&quot;
string s = spec
if exists(spec2) &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec2) != &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec2) != &quot;null&quot;
  s ~= &quot; &quot; ~ spec2
endif
if exists(spec3) &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec3) != &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec3) != &quot;null&quot;
  s ~= &quot; &quot; ~ spec3
endif
strings cv = defarray(&quot;ordinary&quot;, &quot;white&quot;, &quot;hac&quot;)
bundle b = ev_ls(s, vars, cv[cov])    # prints the table into the result window
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__expand_diff" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code># d(Y), d(Y(-k)), dlog(Y), dlog(Y(-k)), d(log(Y)), d(log(Y(-k))) written with
# explicit lags, so that the first observation of the sample uses pre-sample
# data, as EViews does (gretl's diff/ldiff of a lagged series would give NA)
string e = s
string N = &quot;([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)&quot;
loop k = 0..24
  string lk = k ? sprintf(&quot;\(\s*-\s*%d\s*\)&quot;, k) : &quot;&quot;
  string a = k ? sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, k) : &quot;&quot;
  string b2 = sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, k + 1)
  e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])dlog\(\s*&quot; ~ N ~ &quot;\s*&quot; ~ lk ~ &quot;\s*\)&quot;, &quot;(log(\1&quot; ~ a ~ &quot;)-log(\1&quot; ~ b2 ~ &quot;))&quot;)
  e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])d\(\s*log\(\s*&quot; ~ N ~ &quot;\s*&quot; ~ lk ~ &quot;\s*\)\s*\)&quot;, &quot;(log(\1&quot; ~ a ~ &quot;)-log(\1&quot; ~ b2 ~ &quot;))&quot;)
  e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])d\(\s*&quot; ~ N ~ &quot;\s*&quot; ~ lk ~ &quot;\s*\)&quot;, &quot;(\1&quot; ~ a ~ &quot;-\1&quot; ~ b2 ~ &quot;)&quot;)
endloop
return e
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__translate" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code># Rewrite an EViews expression into hansl syntax.
string AT = &quot;@&quot;
string e = ev__expand_diff(s)
# EViews function names -&gt; hansl / package equivalents
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bdlog\(&quot;, &quot;ldiff(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bd\(&quot;, &quot;diff(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\blog\(&quot;, &quot;log(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bexp\(&quot;, &quot;exp(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\babs\(&quot;, &quot;abs(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bsqr\(&quot;, &quot;sqrt(&quot;)
# EViews at-functions
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;trend(\(\))?&quot;, &quot;(obs-1)&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;seas\(&quot;, &quot;ev_seas(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pchy\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pchy(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pcy\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pcy(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pch\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pch(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pc\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pc(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;movav\(&quot;, &quot;ev_movav(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;movsum\(&quot;, &quot;ev_movsum(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;cumsum\(&quot;, &quot;cum(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;mean\(&quot;, &quot;ev_mean(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;stdev\(&quot;, &quot;ev_stdev(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;abs\(&quot;, &quot;abs(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;log\(&quot;, &quot;log(&quot;)
errorif(instring(e, AT), sprintf(&quot;Unsupported EViews function in '%s'&quot;, s))
return e
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__fit" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="Z" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="ssr" type="scalarref"/>
  <param name="df" type="scalarref"/>
 </params>
<code># Least squares via generalized inverse (safe if Z is rank-deficient).
# Returns centered R-squared; fills SSR and rank(Z).
matrix e = y - Z * (ginv(Z'Z) * (Z'y))
ssr = e'e
df = rank(Z)
matrix d = y - meanc(y)
return 1 - ssr / (d'd)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__line" type="void" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="n" type="int" min="1" default="78"/>
 </params>
<code>string s = &quot;&quot;
loop n
  s ~= &quot;=&quot;
endloop
printf &quot;%s\n&quot;, s
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__prep" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="expr" type="string"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
 </params>
<code># EViews expression -&gt; hansl expression in which dataset series are vars.NAME
string evx_e = ev__translate(expr)
strings evx_nms = varnames(vars)
strings evx_ids = strsplit(regsub(evx_e, &quot;[^A-Za-z0-9_]+&quot;, &quot; &quot;))
# Refer to each series as vars.NAME rather than copying it: a copy made
# inside a function holds only in-sample values, while vars.NAME(-k)
# can reach pre-sample observations, as gretl and EViews do for lags.
strings evx_done = array(0)
loop evx_j = 1..nelem(evx_ids)
  string evx_id = evx_ids[evx_j]
  if rows(instrings(evx_nms, evx_id)) &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; rows(instrings(evx_done, evx_id)) == 0
    evx_e = regsub(evx_e, &quot;(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])&quot; ~ evx_id ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;vars.&quot; ~ evx_id)
    evx_done += evx_id
  endif
endloop
return evx_e
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__gen2" type="series" private="1">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="expr" type="string"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="base" type="string"/>
  <param name="dlt" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># like ev_gen, but the dataset series called base is shifted by dlt
# (forecast minus actual; zero before the sample), lags included
string evx_e = ev__prep(expr, vars)
evx_e = regsub(evx_e, &quot;vars\.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(\(-?[0-9]+\))?(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;(vars.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;\1 + misszero(dlt\1))&quot;)
series evx_out = @evx_e
return evx_out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__toseries" type="series" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="tobs" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code>series s = NA
loop i = 1..rows(v)
  scalar t = tobs[i]
  s[t] = v[i]
endloop
return s
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__stats" type="void" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code># common EViews statistics from b.y, b.uhat, b.k, b.lnl (and b.T)
scalar n = rows(b.uhat)
scalar k = b.k
matrix u = b.uhat
matrix d = b.y - meanc(b.y)
b.T = n
b.ssr = u'u
b.rsq = 1 - b.ssr / (d'd)
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - b.rsq) * (n - 1) / (n - k)
b.meany = meanc(b.y)
b.sdy = sqrt(d'd / (n - 1))
scalar kk = inbundle(b, &quot;sigmasq&quot;) ? k + 1 : k
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * kk / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + kk * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * kk * log(log(n)) / n
matrix du = u[2:n] - u[1:n-1]
b.dw = (du'du) / (u'u)
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix p = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  p[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, n - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = p
if !inbundle(b, &quot;F&quot;)
  b.F = NA
  b.Fp = NA
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__depform" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="dep" type="string"/>
  <param name="base" type="stringref"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
 </params>
<code># form of the dependent variable: 0 = Y, 1 = log(Y), 2 = d(Y), 3 = dlog(Y)
# or d(log(Y)); -1 = other. base receives the series name Y.
strings pats = defarray(&quot;^\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*log\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*d\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*dlog\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*d\(\s*log\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*\)\s*$&quot;)
matrix forms = {0, 1, 2, 3, 3}
loop i = 1..nelem(pats)
  string m = regsub(dep, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ pats[i], &quot;\1&quot;)
  if m != dep || i == 1 &amp;&amp; regsub(dep, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ pats[1], &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
    if rows(instrings(varnames(vars), m)) &gt; 0
      base = m
      return forms[i]
    endif
  endif
endloop
base = &quot;&quot;
return -1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__toseries_s" type="series" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="tobs" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(v, tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__fc_finish" type="bundle" private="1">
 <params count="15">
  <param name="b" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="dep" type="string"/>
  <param name="base" type="string"/>
  <param name="form" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool"/>
  <param name="level" type="bool"/>
  <param name="y" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="yf" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="se" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="Ylev" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="yfl" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="sel" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="tobs" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool"/>
  <param name="approx_se" type="bool"/>
 </params>
<code>bundle f
f.depvar = b.depvar
f.base = toupper(base)
f.form = form
f.dynamic = dynamic
f.level = level &amp;&amp; form &gt; 0
f.yf = yf
f.se = se
f.actual = y
f.yfl = yfl
f.sel = sel
f.actual_level = Ylev
f.tobs = tobs
f.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
f.se_note = approx_se ? &quot;S.E. of a dynamic forecast from an explicit equation uses the one-step formula&quot; : &quot;&quot;
# evaluation statistics for the series reported
matrix a = f.level ? Ylev : y
matrix p = f.level ? yfl : yf
matrix m = ok(a) .* ok(p)
f.nobs = sum(m)
if f.nobs &gt; 0
  a = selifr(a, m)
  p = selifr(p, m)
  matrix e = p - a
  scalar mse = meanc(e.^2)
  f.rmse = sqrt(mse)
  f.mae = meanc(abs(e))
  f.mape = 100 * meanc(abs(e ./ a))
  f.theil = f.rmse / (sqrt(meanc(a.^2)) + sqrt(meanc(p.^2)))
  scalar sa = sqrt(meanc((a - meanc(a)).^2))
  scalar sp = sqrt(meanc((p - meanc(p)).^2))
  scalar r = (sa &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; sp &gt; 0) ? meanc((a - meanc(a)) .* (p - meanc(p))) / (sa * sp) : 0
  f.bias_prop = (meanc(p) - meanc(a))^2 / mse
  f.var_prop = (sp - sa)^2 / mse
  f.cov_prop = 2 * (1 - r) * sp * sa / mse
endif
if !quiet
  ev_fprint(&amp;f)
endif
return f
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__fc_arma" type="bundle" private="1">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="b" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool"/>
  <param name="level" type="bool"/>
  <param name="form" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="base" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code># regression with ARMA errors: y = X beta + u,  phi(L) u = theta(L) e
string dep = strsplit(b.spec)[1]
series eva_y = ev_gen(dep, vars)
matrix y = {eva_y}
series eva_o = obs
matrix tobs = {eva_o}
scalar T = rows(y)
matrix Xf = b.hasc ? ones(T, 1) : {}
loop i = 1..nelem(b.xtok)
  series eva_x = ev_gen(b.xtok[i], vars)
  Xf ~= {eva_x}
endloop
matrix xb = cols(Xf) &gt; 0 ? Xf * b.beta : zeros(T, 1)
scalar s0 = tobs[1]
scalar N = max(tobs[T], maxc(b.tobs))
matrix U = mshape(NA, N, 1)        # u = y - X beta, by observation number
matrix E = mshape(NA, N, 1)        # innovations
U[b.tobs] = b.ureg
E[b.tobs] = b.uhat
scalar pmax = cols(b.pl) ? maxr(b.pl) : 0
scalar qmax = cols(b.ql) ? maxr(b.ql) : 0
errorif(s0 - max(pmax, qmax) &lt; minc(b.tobs) || s0 &gt; maxc(b.tobs) + 1, &quot;ARMA forecasts must start inside the estimation sample or right after it&quot;)
# for static forecasts actual u and e inside the forecast sample are needed
matrix uact = y - xb
matrix yf = mshape(NA, T, 1)
loop t = 1..T
  scalar s = tobs[t]
  scalar uh = 0
  loop i = 1..cols(b.pl)
    scalar L = b.pl[i]
    scalar uu = (s - L &lt; s0 || !dynamic) ? U[s - L] : yf[t - L] - xb[t - L]
    if s - L &gt;= s0 &amp;&amp; !dynamic
      uu = uact[t - L]
    endif
    uh += b.phi[i] * uu
  endloop
  loop i = 1..cols(b.ql)
    scalar L = b.ql[i]
    scalar ee = s - L &lt; s0 ? E[s - L] : (dynamic ? 0 : E[s - L])
    uh += b.theta[i] * ee
  endloop
  yf[t] = xb[t] + uh
  if !dynamic
    # one-step innovation at s, used by later static steps
    E[s] = uact[t] - uh
    U[s] = uact[t]
  endif
endloop
# psi weights of the ARMA error process
matrix psi = zeros(T, 1)
psi[1] = 1
loop j = 2..T
  scalar v = 0
  loop i = 1..cols(b.ql)
    if b.ql[i] == j - 1
      v += b.theta[i]
    endif
  endloop
  loop i = 1..cols(b.pl)
    if j - b.pl[i] &gt;= 1
      v += b.phi[i] * psi[j - b.pl[i]]
    endif
  endloop
  psi[j] = v
endloop
matrix psiC = cum(psi)
scalar s2 = b.sigmasq
matrix se = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix Ylev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix Yprev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix yfl = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix sel = mshape(NA, T, 1)
if form &gt;= 0
  string e1 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base
  string e2 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(-1)&quot;
  series evf_L = @e1
  series evf_Lp = @e2
  Ylev = {evf_L}
  Yprev = {evf_Lp}
endif
loop t = 1..T
  scalar h = dynamic ? t : 1
  se[t] = sqrt(s2 * sumc(psi[1:h].^2))
  if form &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; ok(yf[t])
    scalar prev = (t &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; dynamic &amp;&amp; ok(yfl[t-1])) ? yfl[t-1] : Yprev[t]
    if form == 0
      yfl[t] = yf[t]
      sel[t] = se[t]
    elif form == 1
      yfl[t] = exp(yf[t])
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * se[t]
    elif form == 2
      yfl[t] = prev + yf[t]
      sel[t] = dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t]
    else
      yfl[t] = prev * exp(yf[t])
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * (dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t])
    endif
  endif
endloop
return ev__fc_finish(b, dep, base, form, dynamic, level, y, yf, se, Ylev, yfl, sel, tobs, quiet, 0)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__roots" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="coefs" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="lagv" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="sgn" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code># inverted roots of 1 - sgn*sum(coef_i L^lag_i), formatted like EViews
if cols(lagv) == 0
  return &quot;&quot;
endif
scalar p = maxr(lagv)
matrix a = zeros(1, p + 1)
a[1] = 1
loop i = 1..cols(lagv)
  a[lagv[i] + 1] = -sgn * coefs[i]
endloop
matrix r = polroots(a)
matrix rr = iscomplex(r) ? Re(r) : r[,1]
matrix ri = iscomplex(r) ? Im(r) : (cols(r) &gt; 1 ? r[,2] : zeros(rows(r), 1))
string out = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..rows(rr)
  scalar xr = rr[i]
  scalar xi = ri[i]
  scalar m2 = xr^2 + xi^2
  scalar ire = xr / m2
  scalar iim = -xi / m2
  if abs(iim) &lt; 1e-8
    out ~= sprintf(&quot;%10.2f&quot;, ire)
  else
    out ~= sprintf(&quot;%10s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;%.2f%s%.2fi&quot;, ire, iim &gt;= 0 ? &quot;+&quot; : &quot;-&quot;, abs(iim)))
  endif
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<sample-script>
set verbose off
include EViewsCompat.gfn
open denmark --quiet

# EViews:  ls dlog(lrm) c dlog(lry) lrm(-1) ibo ide
bundle eq1 = ev_ls(&quot;dlog(LRM) c dlog(LRY) LRM(-1) IBO IDE&quot;, dataset)

# EViews:  eq1.wald c(4)=0, c(5)=0
bundle w = ev_wald(eq1, &quot;c(4)=0, c(5)=0&quot;)

# EViews:  View &gt; Residual Diagnostics
bundle d = ev_diag(eq1, 2)

# EViews:  White / HAC coefficient covariance
bundle eq2 = ev_ls(&quot;dlog(LRM) c dlog(LRY) LRM(-1)&quot;, dataset, &quot;hac&quot;)

# EViews:  series g = @pch(lry)  /  series sm = @movav(lry, 4)
series g = ev_gen(&quot;@pch(LRY)&quot;, dataset)
series sm = ev_gen(&quot;@movav(LRY, 4)&quot;, dataset)

# EViews:  Freeze the estimation table
ev_freeze(eq1, &quot;eq1.csv&quot;)
</sample-script>
</gretl-function-package>
</gretl-functions>
